# Responsive Layout

All UI must be responsive and adapt to different screen sizes using Tailwind CSS breakpoints.

## Breakpoints (mobile-first)

- Default (no prefix) — mobile, `< 640px`
- `sm:` — `≥ 640px`
- `md:` — `≥ 768px`
- `lg:` — `≥ 1024px`
- `xl:` — `≥ 1280px`

## Rules

- Always design **mobile-first**: start with mobile styles, then override at larger breakpoints.
- Never use fixed pixel widths for layout containers — use `w-full`, `max-w-*`, or responsive fractions.
- Use responsive grid and flex utilities: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`.
- Use responsive typography: `text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg`.
- Ensure touch targets are at least `44px` on mobile (use `min-h-11 min-w-11` or `p-3`).

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fixed width, not responsive
<div className="w-[800px] flex">...</div>

// ✅ GOOD — fluid, responsive layout
<div className="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4">...</div>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hidden content without responsive alternative
<nav className="hidden">...</nav>

// ✅ GOOD — show/hide at appropriate breakpoints
<nav className="hidden md:flex">...</nav>
<MobileMenu className="flex md:hidden" />
```
